==Points of Interest==
===Observatory===

[[File:Mt Moon Observatory Constellations.png|right|thumb|The constellations]]
In the Observatory at night (8pm-5am) the player can use the telescopes to find 8 different Constellations. After finding a constellation the scientist will reward the player with some Stardust. After finding all 8 constellations the player is rewarded with a Comet Shard. The Observatory is linked the finding [[Legendary Pokémon#Mew|Mew]]. [[Legendary Pokémon#Mew|Mew]] can be encountered if the player has at least 20 [[karma]], and has discovered all of the Constellations.

[[File:Minior_Encounter.mp4|right|thumb|The Minior encounter]]
When looking through the telescope, every so often a shooting star will fly past. If it hits the player's cursor a sound effect will play. (The player can move the cursor around to catch the shooting stars; if just waiting still it can take several minutes.) Then after the player stop looking through the telescope, the shooting star will be heard crashing to the ground outside. When inspecting this crashed meteor, the player will encounter a Minior. This event can be repeated, and on all subsequent times the Minior encounter is not guaranteed; there is a chance the player may instead receive a Star Piece or a Comet Shard.
{{Clear}}
===Cloud Puzzle===
In the sky above the map are some clouds with an NPC related to a [[Legendary Pokémon#Meloetta|Legendary Pokémon]] quest, and a TM. The clouds cannot be traversed, except on Mondays between 5am and 10am ([[Time|in-game time]]) when a path of clouds will appear starting from the east side of the map near the [[Type Experts|Flying-Type Expert]]. ''For the cloud path to appear, the map must load during the designated time. The player can enter and leave the Observatory during this time to force the map to reload.''

The Cloud Puzzle requires the player to jump across the clouds while trying to not fall off in order to reach their objective. If the player stays on a smaller cloud for too long they will fall through and have to restart the puzzle.
